# ── macOS metadata ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AppleDouble sidecars. macOS writes these for any file carrying extended
# attributes when the target filesystem cannot store them natively — which is
# exactly what happens on an SMB share. They must never be committed: Claude
# Code refreshes a marketplace by renaming directories, and a leftover ._ file
# makes that rename fail with ENOTEMPTY, wedging the install for whoever clones
# this repo. Regenerate-and-ignore is the only safe posture here.
._*
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.TemporaryItems
.DocumentRevisions-V100

# ── Windows / NAS artefacts (this repo may live on an SMB volume) ─────────────
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
System Volume Information/

# ── Node ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# plugins/tailwind/scripts ships package.json and package-lock.json on purpose;
# installed dependencies are not committed.
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# ── Claude Code runtime artefacts ────────────────────────────────────────────
.in_use/
*.tmp
*.tmp.*

# ── Never commit the private content layer ───────────────────────────────────
# Company-specific knowledge is supplied through plugin config at runtime, not
# bundled. If a content/ or src/ directory ever appears here, it arrived by
# mistake.
content/
src/
